---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="About" description="Semih Buğra Sezer is an AI engineer focused on agentic AI, LLM applications, MCP developer tools and reliable software systems." type="profile">
  <header class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Semih Buğra Sezer</h1>
    <p class="lede">{SITE.role}</p>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am a computer engineering graduate working on applied AI and autonomous agent systems. I design
        agent workflows, developer tools and the backend infrastructure around them. My central question
        is how AI agents can complete useful work without giving up control of state, credentials or production.
      </p>
      <p>
        My practical work has been in backend development and production software — Go, Python, TypeScript and
        Node.js services, React front ends, PostgreSQL and Redis, Docker and CI/CD pipelines. More recently it has
        included Rust for systems and security tooling.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about the parts of engineering that are easy to skip: explicit state, recovery paths, written threat
        models, tests that fail for the right reason, and documentation that states limitations as clearly as
        features. The case studies on this site are written in that spirit — each one says what is unfinished.
      </p>
      <h2>My AI engineering focus</h2>
      <p>
        I work on tool calling and MCP integrations, agent orchestration, task state and recovery,
        and explicit human-approval boundaries. My <a href="/ai-engineering/">AI engineering evidence page</a>
        links those skills to source code and case studies, and distinguishes tested capabilities from future experiments.
      </p>
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Decompose before building.</strong> Write the problem, the boundaries and the failure modes down first.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep decisions deterministic where they can be.</strong> Use models for the parts that genuinely need judgement, and keep them out of the parts that need guarantees.</li>
        <li><strong>Fail closed.</strong> Unknown input, unclear authority and missing evidence are refusals, not guesses.</li>
        <li><strong>Prefer evidence to adjectives.</strong> Measured, dated facts over claims; “not verified” when that is the truth.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Independent research</h2>
      <p>
        “Independent researcher” here means independent technical investigation: questions that come up while
        building systems, explored with a stated method and published with their limitations in the
        <a href="/research/">research journal</a>. I do not hold an academic appointment and none of it is peer-reviewed.
      </p>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p>
        B.Sc. Computer Engineering, Karabük University. Senior project: a performance comparison of network
        topologies and queueing algorithms using NS-3 simulation
        (<a href="https://github.com/semihbugrasezer/network-simulation-dashboard" rel="noopener" target="_blank">results dashboard</a>).
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="side">
      <section>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Working with</h2>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Languages</dt><dd>Go, Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, Rust</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Backend</dt><dd>Node.js, FastAPI, REST, MCP / JSON-RPC</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Data</dt><dd>PostgreSQL, Redis</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Infrastructure</dt><dd>Docker, Compose, Traefik, GitHub Actions, Linux</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Frontend</dt><dd>React</dd></div>
          <div><dt>AI tooling</dt><dd>Claude Code, Codex CLI, LLM APIs</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Elsewhere</h2>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li><a href={SITE.github} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub — semihbugrasezer</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.linkedin} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .grid { display: grid; gap: var(--s-7); padding-top: var(--s-6); }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) { .grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, var(--measure)) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .side { display: grid; gap: var(--s-6); align-content: start; }
  .side dl { display: grid; gap: var(--s-3); margin-top: var(--s-3); }
  .side dt { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .side dd { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .plain { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: var(--s-3); display: grid; gap: var(--s-2); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
</style>
